---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About the Platform & Mission"
  description="Mission, philosophy, and architectural principles of the Interactive CS Visualizers platform."
  currentRoute="/about/"
>
  <div class="content-container">
    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="page-badge">MISSION & PHILOSOPHY</span>
      <h1 class="page-title">ABOUT THE PLATFORM</h1>
      <p class="page-lead">
        “Don't just see the answer — understand how it works.”
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-body">
      <section class="prose-section">
        <h2>1. Why This Platform Exists</h2>
        <p>
          Learning data structures and algorithms is often intimidating. Traditional textbooks show static diagrams, while modern AI tools generate instant answers without teaching the underlying mechanics.
        </p>
        <p>
          This platform was built to bridge that gap for CS/IT students, self-taught developers, and coding interview candidates across the globe. By rendering algorithms as step-by-step, reversible interactive state machines, learners can inspect exactly how pointers move, why swaps occur, and where algorithmic efficiency comes from.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="prose-section">
        <h2>2. Core Architectural Principles</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Zero Data Transmission:</strong> Every calculation, JSON parse, and algorithm step runs 100% inside your local web browser. Your inputs are never transmitted to a server.</li>
          <li><strong>Deterministic Reversibility:</strong> Our step-engine precomputes immutable state snapshots, enabling instant, bug-free backward and forward stepping.</li>
          <li><strong>Plain-English Narration:</strong> Instead of generic status messages, every step explains in clear English what the algorithm is doing and why.</li>
          <li><strong>Zero Account Barrier:</strong> No logins, no paywalls, no tracking cookies, and no third-party telemetry.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="prose-section">
        <h2>3. Target Audience</h2>
        <p>
          Tailored for international English-speaking learners, especially students and aspiring software engineers in India, the United States, the United Kingdom, and worldwide.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .content-container {
    max-width: var(--reading-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-12) var(--gutter);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .page-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .page-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-brand-400);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wider);
  }

  .page-title {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .page-lead {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-emerald-400);
  }

  .prose-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .prose-section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .prose-section h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .prose-section p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .prose-section ul {
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .prose-section li {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .prose-section strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
</style>
